Plan an ID3v2.3 file's original date as the year the file can hold.

Why: on ID3v2.3 the original date is written to TORY, which keeps the year
only (fields.rs Id3Target, id3_edit.rs year_of). The profile planner compared
the release's full date ("2015-01-12") with the "2015" read back, so every
plan saw a change. With automatic management on, each scan re-planned and
rewrote the same albums: measured 2026-10-24, about 15 albums rewritten every
~6 minutes (one 10 times in 100 minutes), each run only "original_date: 2015
-> 2015-01-12". The planner now brings the desired value into TORY's form,
next to the existing "/"-join for v2.3 multi-values.

Tests: new unit test plans a v2.3 file twice; the second plan changes
nothing. It fails without the fix with the loop's own symptom (pass 0 wants
"2015-01-12").

Remove when: upstream compares v2.3 original dates by year.

